# M6 4b (slice 350; slice 303's row in the colon form): a method's name as the left side -- `one: two` in a method --
# is refused at translation, located: only the call mark calls (the author 2026-11-09), so the Frame is the write of
# the place its head names, and a method is no place a statement writes; nothing is called.  Inside a method the head
# `one` is a call head (l2_call_head_method); lm_compiler_is_asgn takes it for a call only with the call mark (slice
# 349), so the check says this refusal instead of binding a call of `one` with the actual `two`.
fn: one () int
    return: 1
end: one
fn: two () int
    return: 2
end: two
fn: f () int
    one: two
    return: 1
end: f
int: code 7
if: f() != 1
    code: 81
---
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: code; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
